Description: Hot cue pads start playback on a paused deck, like a CDJ
 hotcue_X_activate on a paused deck used to *preview* the cue: the deck
 played only while the pad was held, then jumped back to the cue and stopped
 when it was let go, so a tap left the deck paused. A CDJ starts playing from
 the hot cue and keeps playing. CueControl::hotcueActivate() now does that
 when the deck is paused and no preview is running: a hot cue goes through
 hotcueGotoAndPlay() and a saved loop through hotcueGotoAndLoop() (jump to
 the loop start, engage the loop, play). Pads on a playing deck, empty pads
 (set a cue) and a pad pressed during a running preview are unchanged, and
 the preview itself is still reachable as hotcue_X_activate_preview.
 .
 debian/rules runs mixxx-test, so the one test that previewed through
 hotcue_X_activate (EngineSyncTest.QuantizeHotCueActivate, a paused deck)
 now previews through hotcue_1_activate_preview, which runs the same code
 path activate used to; its assertions are unchanged. New tests:
 HotcueControlTest.CueActivateWhilePausedStartsPlayback and
 SavedLoopActivateWhilePausedStartsLoop.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no

